2. EVIDENCE STATUS DEFINITIONS
======================================================================

Each result or result-producing artifact must be assigned one of the
following evidence states.

STATUS A — SPECIFIED

The result or computational quantity is defined in the model or study
protocol but no execution evidence has been established.

STATUS B — DOCUMENTED / REPORTED

The numerical value or graphical representation exists in recovered
documentation, figure, table, workbook, manuscript draft, or note, but
the underlying computational execution artifact has not yet been recovered
or linked.

STATUS C — EXECUTED — EVIDENCE RECOVERED

A corresponding computational execution artifact has been recovered.

Acceptable evidence may include:

- native COMSOL .mph model containing the solution
- COMSOL exported numerical result
- COMSOL solver log
- batch execution record
- patient-specific numerical output
- machine-readable simulation result
- reproducible computational execution record

STATUS D — VERIFIED

The execution artifact exists and the associated result has passed the
applicable verification checks documented in:

09_Stage_3_Verification/

STATUS E — MANUSCRIPT-REPORTED

The result is traceable from patient input through computational execution,
verification, and final result extraction and is therefore suitable for
quantitative reporting in the manuscript.

IMPORTANT:

STATUS B must not automatically become STATUS C.

STATUS C must not automatically become STATUS D.

STATUS D must not automatically become STATUS E.

