25. PROHIBITED RESULT-RECONSTRUCTION PRACTICES
======================================================================

The following are prohibited:

1. Back-calculating patient-level values from group means.

2. Inventing missing COMSOL outputs.

3. Fabricating solver logs.

4. Fabricating verification records.

5. Creating artificial historical execution evidence.

6. Changing numerical values solely to improve figure/table consistency.

7. Treating graphical representations as substitutes for numerical
   execution evidence.

8. Treating planned simulations as executed simulations.

9. Treating documented results as verified results.

10. Treating external reference comparisons as independent validation
    without establishing dataset independence.

11. Reconstructing missing parameters solely to reproduce a desired
    numerical result.

12. Reporting a numerical result as definitive when its provenance is
    unresolved.

